      "source": [
        "# Laboratorio · Variables continuas con NumPy\n",
        "**Simulación de Sistemas · Miércoles 14 de octubre de 2026 · segunda hora**\n",
        "\n",
        "En la primera hora hicimos uniforme, exponencial y normal con `random`. Ahora las comparamos contra las funciones de NumPy. Al final simulamos la ventanilla del banco con 10 clientes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "3b7b6b6b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3b7b6b6b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 0. Preparación\n",
        "Fijamos una semilla para que los resultados se puedan reproducir."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "f701be74",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.263632Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.263345Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.719391Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.718256Z"
        },
        "id": "f701be74"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import math\n",
        "import random\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(2026)\n",
        "print(\"NumPy\", np.__version__)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "0b5590d7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0b5590d7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Repaso: nuestras funciones de la primera hora\n",
        "Estas son las mismas funciones de la presentación, con `random`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "002018f3",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.722011Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.721740Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.726297Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.725568Z"
        },
        "id": "002018f3"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def uniforme(a, b):\n",
        "    return a + (b - a) * random.random()\n",
        "\n",
        "def exponencial(lam):\n",
        "    u = random.random()\n",
        "    return -math.log(1 - u) / lam\n",
        "\n",
        "def normal(mu, sigma):\n",
        "    u1 = random.random()\n",
        "    u2 = random.random()\n",
        "    r = math.sqrt(-2*math.log(1-u1))\n",
        "    z = r * math.cos(2*math.pi*u2)\n",
        "    return mu + sigma * z\n",
        "\n",
        "random.seed(2026)\n",
        "print(uniforme(2, 8), exponencial(0.5), normal(10, 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "33ace1b6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "33ace1b6"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Las funciones de NumPy\n",
        "Ahora generamos 10 000 valores de cada distribución con NumPy.\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Cuidado:** `np.random.exponential` recibe `scale = 1/λ`, no λ. Con λ = 0.5 el `scale` es 2."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "e2f9c1b7",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.728549Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.728320Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.734623Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.733560Z"
        },
        "id": "e2f9c1b7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "N = 10_000\n",
        "lam = 0.5\n",
        "\n",
        "u_np = rng.uniform(2, 8, N)\n",
        "e_np = rng.exponential(scale=1/lam, size=N)   # scale = 1/λ\n",
        "n_np = rng.normal(loc=10, scale=2, size=N)    # loc = μ, scale = σ\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"uniforme   media:\", u_np.mean().round(3))\n",
        "print(\"exponencial media:\", e_np.mean().round(3))\n",
        "print(\"normal     media:\", n_np.mean().round(3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4fa9b718",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4fa9b718"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Validación: media y varianza contra la teoría\n",
        "| Distribución | Media teórica | Varianza teórica |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Uniforme(a, b) | (a + b) / 2 | (b − a)² / 12 |\n",
        "| Exponencial(λ) | 1 / λ | 1 / λ² |\n",
        "| Normal(μ, σ) | μ | σ² |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0316ae79",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.736181Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.735995Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.741839Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.740866Z"
        },
        "id": "0316ae79"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "tabla = [\n",
        "    (\"Uniforme(2,8)\", u_np, 5, 36/12),\n",
        "    (\"Exponencial(λ=0.5)\", e_np, 1/lam, 1/lam**2),\n",
        "    (\"Normal(10,2)\", n_np, 10, 4),\n",
        "]\n",
        "for nombre, datos, media_t, var_t in tabla:\n",
        "    print(f\"{nombre:22s} media {datos.mean():7.3f} (teórica {media_t:6.3f})   \"\n",
        "          f\"varianza {datos.var():7.3f} (teórica {var_t:6.3f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ead9c6bc",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ead9c6bc"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Histogramas lado a lado\n",
        "Nuestra función (`random`) contra la de NumPy, para cada distribución."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "1e8f48dd",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.743671Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-13T19:11:54.743452Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-13T19:11:55.506897Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-13T19:11:55.506200Z"
        },
        "id": "1e8f48dd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "random.seed(7)\n",
        "nuestra = {\n",
        "    \"uniforme\": [uniforme(2, 8) for _ in range(N)],\n",
        "    \"exponencial\": [exponencial(lam) for _ in range(N)],\n",
        "    \"normal\": [normal(10, 2) for _ in range(N)],\n",
        "}\n",
        "numpy_ = {\"uniforme\": u_np, \"exponencial\": e_np, \"normal\": n_np}\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ejes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "for j, k in enumerate(nuestra):\n",
        "    ejes[0, j].hist(nuestra[k], bins=40, color=\"#306998\")\n",
        "    ejes[0, j].set_title(f\"{k}: nuestra (random)\")\n",
        "    ejes[1, j].hist(numpy_[k], bins=40, color=\"#FFD43B\", edgecolor=\"#8a7400\")\n",
        "    ejes[1, j].set_title(f\"{k}: NumPy\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cd30cfe4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cd30cfe4"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Ejercicio de cierre: la ventanilla\n",
        "Un banco tiene una sola ventanilla.\n",
        "- Llegadas: tiempo entre llegadas exponencial con media de 2 minutos.\n",
        "- Servicio: tiempo de atención uniforme entre 1 y 4 minutos.\n",
        "- Cada cliente espera su turno: inicio = el mayor entre su llegada y el fin del cliente anterior.\n",
        "\n",
        "Simulamos 10 clientes en cada corrida y repetimos 1 000 corridas."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "b8f954d2",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-13T19:11:55.509306Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-13T19:11:55.508947Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-13T19:11:55.529081Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-13T19:11:55.528291Z"
        },
        "id": "b8f954d2",
        "outputId": "b2cf7859-68e0-473c-a185-a74aa5cc794c",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Espera promedio por cliente, promedio de 1 000 corridas: 5.492 min\n",
            "Desviación entre corridas: 2.639 min\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def corrida(n_clientes=10):\n",
        "    entre_llegadas = rng.exponential(scale=2, size=n_clientes)\n",
        "    servicio = rng.uniform(1, 5, size=n_clientes)\n",
        "    llegada = np.cumsum(entre_llegadas)    # minuto en que llega cada cliente\n",
        "    inicio = np.empty(n_clientes)\n",
        "    fin = np.empty(n_clientes)\n",
        "    for i in range(n_clientes):\n",
        "        inicio[i] = max(llegada[i], fin[i-1]) if i > 0 else llegada[i]\n",
        "        fin[i] = inicio[i] + servicio[i]\n",
        "    espera = inicio - llegada\n",
        "    return espera.mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "esperas = np.array([corrida() for _ in range(1000)])\n",
        "print(\"Espera promedio por cliente, promedio de 1 000 corridas:\", esperas.mean().round(3), \"min\")\n",
        "print(\"Desviación entre corridas:\", esperas.std().round(3), \"min\")"
      ]
    },
    {
